  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'It has been days since I came back, and no one is here.


    I used to
    think I was the victim.

    I used to think my family were the ones ruining
    my life.


    I blamed them for my anger, my suffocation, and every choice I
    could not make.


    I thought they were stealing my freedom from me.

    Now
    I know the truth.


    They loved me, and I answered that love with pride.


    They
    warned me, and I called it control.


    They feared for me, and I called it
    oppression.


    I was so certain that leaving them would finally make me a
    man. I thought choosing my own life meant I had won. But the life I fought for
    collapsed in my own hands, and the people I turned against were the only ones
    who had ever truly cared whether I stood or fell.


    I came back wanting to
    say I was sorry.

    I came back wanting to ask my mother to forgive me.

    I
    came back wanting to look my father in the face and admit that I was wrong.


    I
    came back wanting to tell my brother and sister that I never stopped loving them,
    even when I acted like I did.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
